{
    "title": "Arabvia",
    "description": "Be Safe Co. developed the Arabvia application as a free application that aims to provide a safe and improved experience for users. This Privacy Policy describes our commitment to protecting your personal information, and ensuring transparency about how we collect, use and disclose your data when you use our Services.\r\n\r\nWhen you choose to use the Arabvia application, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. The Personal Data we collect is mainly used to improve the Service. We are committed not to share your information with third parties, except as described in this Privacy Policy.\r\n\r\nInformation Collection and Use: To improve your experience, we may request personal information, which will be held and used in accordance with this policy. The app uses third-party services such as Google Play Services, Google Analytics for Firebase, Firebase Crashlytics, Facebook, and One Signal, which may collect data to identify you.\r\n\r\nLog Data: In case of errors, we collect data such as your IP address, device name, operating system version, application configuration, time and date of use. This information helps us understand and improve the application.\r\n\r\nCookies: While the application itself does not use cookies, external code and libraries within the application may use these cookies to collect information and improve its services. You can accept or decline cookies, but declining may limit some functionality of the Service.\r\n\r\nService Providers: We may employ third-party companies to facilitate our Services, provide services on our behalf, or help analyze how the Service is used. These providers obtain your personal information only to perform their functions and are prohibited from disclosure or use for any other purposes.\r\n\r\nSecurity: We place a premium on protecting your personal information using commercially acceptable security measures. However, you should remember that no method of transmitting data over the Internet or storing it electronically is 100% secure and we cannot guarantee its complete security.\r\n\r\nLinks to other sites: The Arabvia application may contain links to external sites, which are not operated by us. We strongly advise you to review the privacy policies of those sites, as we have no control over their content or practices.\r\n\r\nChildren's Privacy: Arabvia does not target anyone under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect data from children under 13. If we are discovered to have provided this data to a child, we delete it immediately. If you are a parent or guardian and you learn that your child has provided us with personal data, please contact us for necessary actions.\r\n\r\nPolicy Updates: We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Users are advised to check this page for any changes. Notices of updates will be posted here.\r\n\r\nFor any questions or suggestions about our privacy policy, please contact us at arabvia.com. This policy is effective as of July 10, 2024.",
    "descriptionHTML": "Be Safe Co. developed the Arabvia application as a free application that aims to provide a safe and improved experience for users. This Privacy Policy describes our commitment to protecting your personal information, and ensuring transparency about how we collect, use and disclose your data when you use our Services.<br><br>When you choose to use the Arabvia application, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. The Personal Data we collect is mainly used to improve the Service. We are committed not to share your information with third parties, except as described in this Privacy Policy.<br><br>Information Collection and Use: To improve your experience, we may request personal information, which will be held and used in accordance with this policy. The app uses third-party services such as Google Play Services, Google Analytics for Firebase, Firebase Crashlytics, Facebook, and One Signal, which may collect data to identify you.<br><br>Log Data: In case of errors, we collect data such as your IP address, device name, operating system version, application configuration, time and date of use. This information helps us understand and improve the application.<br><br>Cookies: While the application itself does not use cookies, external code and libraries within the application may use these cookies to collect information and improve its services. You can accept or decline cookies, but declining may limit some functionality of the Service.<br><br>Service Providers: We may employ third-party companies to facilitate our Services, provide services on our behalf, or help analyze how the Service is used. These providers obtain your personal information only to perform their functions and are prohibited from disclosure or use for any other purposes.<br><br>Security: We place a premium on protecting your personal information using commercially acceptable security measures. However, you should remember that no method of transmitting data over the Internet or storing it electronically is 100% secure and we cannot guarantee its complete security.<br><br>Links to other sites: The Arabvia application may contain links to external sites, which are not operated by us. We strongly advise you to review the privacy policies of those sites, as we have no control over their content or practices.<br><br>Children&#39;s Privacy: Arabvia does not target anyone under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect data from children under 13. If we are discovered to have provided this data to a child, we delete it immediately. If you are a parent or guardian and you learn that your child has provided us with personal data, please contact us for necessary actions.<br><br>Policy Updates: We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Users are advised to check this page for any changes. Notices of updates will be posted here.<br><br>For any questions or suggestions about our privacy policy, please contact us at arabvia.com. This policy is effective as of July 10, 2024.",
